In the United States, the song debuted at number 92 on the [[Billboard Hot 100|''Billboard'' Hot 100]] for the week of January 3, 2009, and reached number six on March 7 of that year.<ref name="florida">{{cite magazine |last=Ben-Yehuda |first=Ayala |date=February 26, 2009 |title=Flo Rida, T.I. Hold Their Billboard Hot 100 Spots |url=https://www.billboard.com/biz/articles/news/1273893/flo-rida-ti-hold-their-billboard-hot-100-spots |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130522145554/http://www.billboard.com/biz/articles/news/1273893/flo-rida-ti-hold-their-billboard-hot-100-spots |archive-date=May 22, 2013 |access-date=February 26, 2009 |magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]}}</ref> The next week, the song climbed another three places, reaching the number three position and staying there for two additional weeks.<ref name="soulja">{{cite magazine |last=Ben-Yehuda |first=Ayala |date=March 5, 2009 |title=Soulja Boy Climbs Hot 100 |url=https://www.billboard.com/articles/news/269283/soulja-boy-climbs-hot-100 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130524031917/http://www.billboard.com/articles/news/269283/soulja-boy-climbs-hot-100 |archive-date=May 24, 2013 |access-date=March 4, 2009 |magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]}}</ref> On the ''Billboard'' issue dated April 11, 2009, the song topped the chart.<ref name="pair">{{cite magazine |author=Pietroluongo, Silvio |date=April 1, 2009 |title=Lady GaGa Draws A Pair Of No. 1s |url=https://www.billboard.com/articles/news/269065/lady-gaga-draws-a-pair-of-no-1s |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130922174639/http://www.billboard.com/articles/news/269065/lady-gaga-draws-a-pair-of-no-1s |archive-date=September 22, 2013 |access-date=April 1, 2009 |magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]}}</ref> "Poker Face" became Gaga's second consecutive number one song on the ''Billboard'' Hot 100, marking the first time a new artist has had their first two charting singles hit number one on that chart since [[Christina Aguilera]] did so with "[[Genie in a Bottle]]" and "[[What a Girl Wants (Christina Aguilera song)|What a Girl Wants]]" in 1999 and 2000.<ref>{{cite magazine |last=Ben-Yehuda |first=Ayala |author2=Silvio Pietroluongo |date=April 2, 2009 |title=Lady GaGa Scores Hot 100 Milestone With 'Poker Face' |url=https://www.billboard.com/articles/news/269058/lady-gaga-scores-hot-100-milestone-with-poker-face |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130925053438/http://www.billboard.com/articles/news/269058/lady-gaga-scores-hot-100-milestone-with-poker-face |archive-date=September 25, 2013 |access-date=April 2, 2009 |magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]}}</ref> The song spent one week at the top of the chart, nine weeks at number two, 18 weeks in the Top 10 and stayed on the Hot 100 for a total of 40 weeks. "Poker Face" also peaked on both the [[Hot Dance Airplay]] and [[Hot Dance Club Play]] charts.<ref name="hotdance" /> It became the first single since [[Madonna]]'s 2006 single "[[Sorry (Madonna song)|Sorry]]" to top all the three dance charts in a single week including the [[Hot Dance Singles Sales]] chart.<ref>{{cite magazine |last=Bronson |first=Fred |date=February 13, 2009 |title=Chart Beat Chat: Al Green, Lady Gaga, Triple A Chart |url=https://www.billboard.com/bbcom/news/chart-beat-chat-al-green-lady-gaga-triple-1003941564.story |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20100516173424/http://www.billboard.com/news/chart-beat-chat-al-green-lady-gaga-triple-1003941564.story |archive-date=May 16, 2010 |access-date=March 18, 2009 |magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]}}</ref> The song has been certified Diamond by the [[Recording Industry Association of America]] (RIAA), and sold 7.5 million paid digital downloads in the United States as of February 2018, according to [[Nielsen SoundScan]].<ref name="uscareersales18">{{cite magazine |last=Trust |first=Gary |date=February 25, 2018 |title=Ask Billboard: Lady Gaga's Career Sales, The Biggest No. 2 Hits & Ed Sheeran's Latest Chart Record |url=https://www.billboard.com/articles/columns/chart-beat/8218920/-lady-gaga-sales-number-2-hot-100-hits-ed-sheeran-record-ask-billboard |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180225194118/https://www.billboard.com/articles/columns/chart-beat/8218920/-lady-gaga-sales-number-2-hot-100-hits-ed-sheeran-record-ask-billboard |archive-date=February 25, 2018 |access-date=February 25, 2018 |magazine=Billboard}}</ref> Gaga is the first artist in digital history to top the six and seven million mark in paid downloads with two songs, the first being "[[Just Dance (song)|Just Dance]]".<ref name="riaa" /><ref name="2013us">{{cite magazine |date=January 1, 2014 |title=Nielsen & Billboard's 2013 U.S. Music Report |url=http://radioinkmedia.intertechmedia.com/nielsen.pdf |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140109094950/http://radioinkmedia.intertechmedia.com/nielsen.pdf |archive-date=January 9, 2014 |access-date=January 8, 2014 |magazine=Billboard}}</ref> "Poker Face" is Gaga's most digitally-sold track in the United States.<ref>{{cite magazine |last=Trust |first=Gary |date=March 30, 2014 |title=Ask Billboard: Lady Gaga's Biggest Hot 100 Hits |url=https://www.billboard.com/pro/ask-billboard-lady-gagas-biggest-hot-100-hits/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140705064639/http://www.billboard.com/articles/columns/chart-beat/6029335/ask-billboard-lady-gagas-biggest-hot-100-hits |archive-date=July 5, 2014 |access-date=June 4, 2014 |magazine=Billboard}}</ref>

In Canada, the song debuted at number 41 on the [[Canadian Hot 100]]. On the chart dated December 13, 2008, "Poker Face" ascended to the number one spot and then spent nine non-consecutive weeks at the top.<ref name="can" /> The song was later certified Diamond by [[Music Canada]] for sales of 800,000 copies.<ref name="canadacert" /> "Poker Face" entered the Australian charts at number 26, and in its seventh week peaked at number one.<ref name="aus" /> "Poker Face" has shipped over 1,050,000 copies in Australia, being certified fifteen times [[List of music recording certifications|platinum]] by the [[Australian Recording Industry Association]] (ARIA).<ref name="ariacert" /> It held the record for the longest-charting song in [[ARIA Chart]] history of 106 weeks until this was broken in May 2015 by [[Vance Joy]]'s "[[Riptide (Vance Joy song)|Riptide]]".<ref>{{cite web |last=Adams |first=Cameron |date=May 10, 2015 |title=Vance Joy's Riptide breaks Lady Gaga's incredible record on the Australian charts |url=http://www.heraldsun.com.au/entertainment/music/vance-joys-riptide-breaks-lady-gagas-incredible-record-on-the-australian-charts/story-fni0bvjn-1227349125707 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130921061653/https://itunes.apple.com/de/album/poker-face-remixes-ep/id319545941?l=en |archive-date=September 21, 2013 |access-date=May 10, 2015 |work=Herald Sun}}</ref> In New Zealand, the song debuted on the official chart at number 21. In its sixth week, it peaked on the chart, spending 10 consecutive weeks at number one.<ref name="nz" /> "Poker Face" was later certified quintuple platinum, selling over 150,000 copies according to the [[Recording Industry Association of New Zealand]] (RIANZ).<ref name="rianz" />

In the United Kingdom, "Poker Face" debuted at number 30 on the [[UK Singles Chart]]. After three months, it climbed to number one and provided Gaga with her second consecutive British number one single.<ref>{{cite web |title=POKER FACE – LADY GAGA |url=https://www.officialcharts.com/songs/lady-gaga-poker-face/ |access-date=December 16, 2023 |website=Official Charts (UK) |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231216062729/https://www.officialcharts.com/songs/lady-gaga-poker-face/ |archive-date=December 16, 2023 |url-status=live}}</ref> It was the biggest-selling digital single in the United Kingdom, before being overtaken by "[[I Gotta Feeling]]" by [[The Black Eyed Peas]] in June 2010.<ref>{{cite news |last=Taylor |first=Geoff |date=October 23, 2009 |title=2009 Is Record Year For UK Singles Sales |url=http://www.bpi.co.uk/press-area/news-amp3b-press-release/article/2009-is-record-year-for-uk-singles-sales.aspx |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20091027052342/http://www.bpi.co.uk/press-area/news-amp3b-press-release/article/2009-is-record-year-for-uk-singles-sales.aspx |archive-date=October 27, 2009 |access-date=November 3, 2009 |publisher=[[British Phonographic Industry]]}}</ref> However, the song became the country's biggest-selling single of 2009, and was awarded [[The Record of the Year#2009|The Record of the Year]].<ref name="pfuk">{{cite news |last=Gilbert |first=Ben |date=December 1, 2009 |title=Top 10 best-selling singles of 2009 |url=http://uk.yearinreview.yahoo.com/2009/blog/13 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20091206065759/http://uk.yearinreview.yahoo.com/2009/blog/13 |archive-date=December 6, 2009 |access-date=December 20, 2009 |publisher=[[Yahoo!]]}}</ref> By September 2017 the song had 1.18 million pure sales and had been streamed 8.27 million times.<ref name="uksales">{{cite web |last=Copsey |first=Rob |date=September 19, 2017 |title=The UK's Official Chart 'millionaires' revealed |url=http://www.officialcharts.com/chart-news/the-uks-official-chart-millionaires-revealed__20459/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170919122703/http://www.officialcharts.com/chart-news/the-uks-official-chart-millionaires-revealed__20459/ |archive-date=September 19, 2017 |access-date=September 19, 2017 |publisher=Official Charts Company}}</ref> In January 2025, the song was awarded a quadruple platinum certification from the [[British Phonographic Industry]] (BPI) having sold 2.4 million copies in the UK with 155 million streams as of February 2025.<ref name="uksales2025">{{cite web |author1=George Griffiths |title=Lady Gaga's Official Top 40 biggest songs in the UK |url=https://www.officialcharts.com/chart-news/lady-gagas-top-40-biggest-songs-on-the-official-uk-chart__29864/ |access-date=7 February 2025 |website=[[Official Charts Company|Official Charts]] |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200529145041/https://www.officialcharts.com/chart-news/lady-gagas-top-40-biggest-songs-on-the-official-uk-chart__29864/ |archive-date=May 29, 2020 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="bpi" /><ref name="LGtop40">{{Cite web |title=Lady Gaga's Official Top 40 biggest songs in the UK |url=https://www.officialcharts.com/chart-news/lady-gagas-top-40-biggest-songs-on-the-official-uk-chart__29864/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200529145041/https://www.officialcharts.com/chart-news/lady-gagas-top-40-biggest-songs-on-the-official-uk-chart__29864/ |archive-date=May 29, 2020 |access-date=2022-07-25 |website=www.officialcharts.com |language=en}}</ref>

In Italy, the song debuted at number 19 and peaked at number two.<ref name="ita" /> The song has also reached the peak in a number of European countries including Austria, Belgium (Flanders and Wallonia), Denmark, Finland, France, Germany, Ireland, Netherlands, Norway, Poland, Sweden and Switzerland.<ref name="fla" /><ref name="ire" /> In Germany, "Poker Face" became the most successful download single ever and the first to sell more than 500,000 downloads.<ref>{{cite web |title="Poker Face" knackt 500.000er-Download-Marke |url=http://www.gfk-entertainment.com/news/poker-face-knackt-500000er-download-marke.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20141129073337/http://www.gfk-entertainment.com/news/poker-face-knackt-500000er-download-marke.html |archive-date=November 29, 2014 |access-date=November 5, 2012 |publisher=Media Control Charts}}</ref> The song also spent 16 non-consecutive weeks atop the ''Billboard'' [[European Hot 100 Singles]] chart.<ref name="european" /> By November 2009, the song had sold over 9.8 million copies globally according to [[International Federation of the Phonographic Industry|IFPI]], making it the world's best-selling overall single that year.<ref name="ifpi2010">{{cite web |title=Top 10 Digital Songs 2009 |url=http://www.ifpi.org/content/library/dmr2010.pdf |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120122170638/http://www.ifpi.org/content/library/dmr2010.pdf |archive-date=January 22, 2012 |access-date=January 15, 2012 |publisher=[[International Federation of the Phonographic Industry]] |page=7}}</ref> It went on to sell over 13.4 million copies by 2013, making it one of the [[List of best-selling singles|best-selling singles ever]].<ref name="ifpi2010" /><ref name="Poker Face North American single sales 2009-2013">{{cite news |last=Montgomery |first=James |date=December 9, 2009 |title=Eminem Is The Best-Selling Artist Of The Decade |url=http://www.mtv.com/news/articles/1627833/20091208/eminem.jhtml |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20091213043431/http://www.mtv.com/news/articles/1627833/20091208/eminem.jhtml |archive-date=December 13, 2009 |access-date=December 11, 2009 |publisher=[[MTV]]}}
